# Run output is the likeliest place an individual's details end up: personalising
# output is often the point of the work. So runs/ is excluded by default.
#
# The exception has to re-include DIRECTORIES first — git will not descend into
# an excluded directory, so a bare `!runs/*.public.md` never reaches a nested
# file, and the documented escape hatch silently did nothing.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/README.md
!runs/**/*.public.md

# Per-working-copy state. Gitignored is what makes it per-clone: a fresh clone
# has none, which is how the session hook knows it is your first session here.
.harness/local/

# Anything under a personal/ or private/ path, anywhere. Unconditional, and
# checked by scripts/gates/data-boundary.sh — ignoring is a convenience, the
# gate is the rule. Codify BEFORE the first commit: history is not removable
# without a force-push, and by then other people have cloned it.
**/personal/
**/private/

.env
.env.*
!.env.sample
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
.npmrc
.pypirc
.netrc
.DS_Store
